# SYNTHETIC, not a real connector. Exercises the ONE arm of
# `resolve_group` (src/form_schema.rs) that no other fixture reaches:
# `GroupDescriptor.declared == false` (phase F item W4,
# contreforts/contreforts-core#34; gap found in review, a3).
#
# WHY A SECOND UNRESOLVED-GROUP FIXTURE, next to
# dangling-group-reference.ttl: that file's `dangling:PhantomGroup` is
# never typed a sh:PropertyGroup AND carries no rdfs:label and no
# sh:order, so the label/order check catches it first and the
# `!group.declared` branch above it is shadowed. Deleting that branch
# outright left the whole 36-test suite green -- measured -- which makes
# it exactly the "an error arm no input reaches is not a guarantee, it is
# unreviewed code" case this item's own tests are written against.
#
# `undeclared:LooksLikeAGroup` below is the input that separates the two
# checks: it carries a real rdfs:label AND a real sh:order, so the
# label/order check would pass it, and the ONLY thing wrong with it is
# that nothing ever types it `a sh:PropertyGroup`. W2
# (contreforts/contreforts-core#33) added `GroupDescriptor.declared`
# precisely so this is recoverable; without this fixture, nothing proved
# the digest reads it.
#
# Zero such references exist tree-wide: all 17 groups the 45 real
# top-level properties name are typed a sh:PropertyGroup and carry both an
# rdfs:label and an sh:order (measured over the seven declaration.ttl
# files), so rejecting this costs no real connector anything.
@prefix rdfs:         <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sh:           <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd:          <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix contreforts:  <https://contreforts.ds-labs.org/ontologies/declaration#> .
@prefix undeclared:   <https://contreforts.ds-labs.org/ontologies/undeclared-group-test#> .

undeclared:UndeclaredGroupConnectorShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass undeclared:UndeclaredGroupConnector ;
    contreforts:category "test-only" ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path undeclared:label ;
        sh:name "Label" ;
        sh:datatype xsd:string ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:order 1 ;
        sh:group undeclared:LooksLikeAGroup ;
    ] .

# Deliberately NOT `a sh:PropertyGroup`. Everything else a real group
# carries is present, so only `GroupDescriptor.declared` can tell this
# apart from a well-formed one.
undeclared:LooksLikeAGroup
    rdfs:label "Looks Like A Group" ;
    sh:order 1 .
